    <edge source="Crop:infected wheat grains" target="Contaminant:mycotoxins" id="candidate-b94349abb8c91a8caf655379f2989657">
      <data key="d2">candidate-b94349abb8c91a8caf655379f2989657</data>
      <data key="d3">may_contain</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborated</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">0</data>
      <data key="d7">Fusarium head blight is a primary concern because mycotoxins may be produced in infected grains.</data>
      <data key="d8">conditional</data>
      <data key="d9">{"crop_or_species": "wheat", "population": "", "condition": "Fusarium head blight infection", "comparator": "", "metric": ""}</data>
      <data key="d10">True</data>
      <data key="d11">3</data>
      <data key="d12">supported</data>
      <data key="d13">3</data>
      <data key="d14">0</data>
      <data key="d15">evidence_balance_not_probability</data>
      <data key="d16">Crop health and its global impacts on the components of food security</data>
      <data key="d17">FHB does cause important yield reductions, but the disease has become a primary concern because of the mycotoxins that may be produced in infected grains (Parry et al. 1995; McMullen et al. 1997;X u 2003; Xu and Nicholson 2009; Bateman et al. 2007).</data>
    </edge>
